{
  // SECURITY: `create` is now scoped to the caller's OWN employee_id (same
  // pattern as AttendanceRecord) — EmployeeProfile.jsx (the only client
  // caller) always uploads to the caller's own employee record, so a
  // company_id-only rule let any coworker upload a document into someone
  // else's file. `update` is now service-role only (no client code calls
  // entities.EmployeeDocument.update at all).
  //
  // SECURITY (2, RADAR audit 2026-08-03): `read` narrowed from company-wide
  // to the caller's OWN employee_id (same $and shape as `create`) plus the
  // service-role branch. Unlike ShiftTemplate/Holiday (non-sensitive,
  // legitimately company-wide), this entity holds actual personal documents
  // (ID, contracts — see `file_uri`/`name`), and EmployeeProfile.jsx (the
  // only reader) always filters by the caller's own employee.id. A
  // company_id-only read rule let ANY employee in the company read ANY
  // coworker's uploaded documents by passing a different employee_id to
  // entities.EmployeeDocument.filter() directly — a PII exposure with no
  // offsetting product feature (there is no manager-facing document review
  // UI in src/ today). If/when such a UI is built, extend this rule with a
  // role-checked read path (mirroring the manager-only write functions)
  // rather than reopening it to company-wide.
  //
  // SECURITY (3, scheduled audit 2026-09-14): `file_url` renamed to
  // `file_uri`. The row-level RLS above was always correct, but the field
  // held the return value of `Core.UploadFile`, which writes to permanent,
  // world-readable PUBLIC storage — so the metadata row was access-controlled
  // while the document bytes it pointed at were not (Base44's own security
  // scan flagged this: src/pages/EmployeeProfile.jsx uploads HR documents —
  // IDs, contracts — as public files). EmployeeProfile.jsx now uploads via
  // `Core.UploadPrivateFile` (private storage) and stores the resulting
  // `file_uri`, then calls `Core.CreateFileSignedUrl` for a short-lived link
  // each time a document is opened, rather than embedding a permanent public
  // URL. Safe to rename outright rather than dual-write/migrate: the live
  // schema had 0 EmployeeDocument rows at the time of this fix (confirmed via
  // query_entities), so there is no existing `file_url` data to carry over.
  "name": "EmployeeDocument",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "employee_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "company_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "name": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "file_uri": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "URI in Base44 private storage (Core.UploadPrivateFile). NOT a fetchable URL — resolve a temporary one via Core.CreateFileSignedUrl before opening."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "employee_id",
    "company_id",
    "name",
    "file_uri"
  ],
  "rls": {
    "read": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "$and": [
            { "data.company_id": "{{user.data.company_id}}" },
            { "data.employee_id": "{{user.data.employee_id}}" }
          ]
        },
        { "user_condition": { "role": "admin" } }
      ]
    },
    "create": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "$and": [
            { "data.company_id": "{{user.data.company_id}}" },
            { "data.employee_id": "{{user.data.employee_id}}" }
          ]
        },
        { "user_condition": { "role": "admin" } }
      ]
    },
    "update": {
      "user_condition": { "role": "admin" }
    },
    "delete": {
      "user_condition": { "role": "admin" }
    }
  }
}
